ship, but sometimes not good at taking criticism, can be unorganized.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, but can be grumpy, uncooperative.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere, but difficulty communicating, egocentric, not willing to further education.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, but regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership.\n\nWe need to weigh criteria: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, attention, crew cooperation, communication, responsibility, adaptability.\n\nCandidate C: reliability high, decision quality high, crew cooperation positive, but communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education (adaptability). So concerns on communication and adaptability.\n\nCandidate B: stress resilience high, conscientious (reliability), good weather assessment (technical), computer skills (technical), but uncooperative and grumpy (crew cooperation, communication). So concerns on cooperation.\n\nCandidate A: anticipates danger (decision quality), sees complex connections (technical), spatial vision (technical), leadership (crew), but unorganized (attention), not good at criticism (adaptability), maybe reliability issues.\n\nCandidate D: problem solving, concentration, responsibility, but arrogance (crew cooperation), weak leadership, maybe okay on reliability.\n\nWhich is best overall? Hard. Candidate C seems strong on reliability and decision, but communication issues could be serious for cockpit. Candidate B strong on stress and technical, but uncooperative also serious. Candidate A strong on anticipation and technical, but unorganized and criticism issues. Candidate D strong on problem solving and responsibility, but arrogance and weak leadership.\n\nProbably Candidate C is best overall despite communication concerns, because reliability and decision quality are critical. But we need to discuss others. We'll vote for Candidate C, but note we need to discuss others.\n\nThus public message: state recommendation for Candidate C, reference that we are starting discussion, give evidence, explain why we think C is leading, but note concerns.\n\nWe also need to fill METADATA_JSON with vote.\n\nProceed."}
