es. C's reliability is stronger. So likely C remains best. So we keep vote for C, but bring D into discussion.\n\nThus public message: \"I agree with Agent 3 that we still favor C, but we need to evaluate D. D shows strong problem solving, concentration, responsibility, and can respond to unexpected events, indicating good stress resilience and technical competence. However, being seen as a know-it-all and having a hot temper raises serious crew cooperation and communication concerns. Compared to C, D lacks the proven reliability and positive crew atmosphere, and his interpersonal issues may be more severe. Therefore I maintain my provisional vote for Candidate C, but suggest we discuss D's crew cooperation further.\"\n\nWe must include explicit facts: \"responds to unexpected events adequately\", \"can concentrate very well\", \"solves problems extremely well\", \"takes responsibility seriously\", \"regarded as a know-it-all\", \"has a hot temper\". Also reference prior discussion about needing to discuss D.\n\nNow metadata: vote \"Candidate C\"."}
